---
import ServicePage from '../../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { pairs } from '../../i18n/ui';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Why do you not offer sessions?',
    a: 'Because the written form carries more for this work. You get something you can hold on to, and I can work more carefully than an appointment allows.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which language will my interpretation be in?',
    a: 'The language you write to me in. English or German. In German I also follow your lead on register: if you write to me with du, your interpretation comes back in du.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I send more than one dream?',
    a: 'Yes, and from the second one on it gets more interesting. Dreams work in series. Once I have two or three from you, a picture forms that a single dream cannot show yet.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to my dream?',
    a: 'It stays between us. I do not publish what people entrust to me.',
  },
];
---

<ServicePage
  title="Written Dream Interpretation as a Document"
  description="Written dream interpretation with the Aisling Method. Five to ten pages as a finished PDF. No appointment, no time pressure. 29 € instead of 69 €."
  path="/en/written-dream-interpretation"
  alternates={pairs.written}
  lang="en"
  h1="Written dream interpretation"
  lead="Your interpretation as a document, not an appointment. To read back, to put down, to find again in six months."
  serviceName="Written dream interpretation with the Aisling Method"
  faq={faq}>

  <h2>Why in writing</h2>
  <p>
    Almost everyone who offers dream interpretation does it in conversation. An
    appointment, an hour, and then it is over. I work differently on purpose,
    and the reasons have to do with you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>You do not have to react on the spot.</strong> In a conversation you
    are sitting there expected to place what you are hearing in the same moment.
    Some of it does not land at all, because you are still on the previous
    sentence. A text waits for you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>You can read it again.</strong> In my experience the part that fits
    announces itself a few days later on its own, often at some everyday moment
    you would never have connected it to. That is when you want to be able to
    read it back. A conversation is gone.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>I can work unhurried.</strong> A line by line interpretation takes
    time. In a conversation it happens under time pressure, and the places where
    I would want to go back over something fall by the wayside. Writing lets me
    do that.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>It is easier to write a dream down than to tell it.</strong>
    Especially dreams that were unpleasant. Writing takes part of the hurdle
    away.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <p>
    Five to ten pages, as a professionally typeset, print-ready PDF. Built
    according to the Aisling Method:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your dream in your own words, with its context</li>
    <li>The core theme of the dream</li>
    <li>I AM and I SHOULD, from your own perspective</li>
    <li>The line by line interpretation</li>
    <li>Symbols, colours, places and numbers</li>
    <li>A word of reassurance, where the dream was dark</li>
    <li>A closing reflection and concrete next steps</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can see what that looks like before you decide:
    <a href="/en/example-interpretation">a full interpretation, start to finish</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>And if I still have questions</h2>
  <p>
    Then write to me. After the interpretation I check in anyway to ask whether
    it reached you. If something stays unclear, or you see it differently, that
    matters and is part of the work. The text is not a verdict but an offer:
    take what lands with you, and leave what feels foreign. You know your life,
    I only know this one dream.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>29 € instead of 69 €</strong> as an introductory offer. As a small
    business under §19 UStG, no VAT is charged. Payment runs through a secure
    payment link, straightforward from Austria and Switzerland too.
  </p>

</ServicePage>
